 {"id":"fabro-ff7a","title":"Route no-change verification resubmits straight to reviewer","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:44.366Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:44.366Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro, add an 'Implemented (no changes)' label edge from implementer directly to reviewer, or condition the tester edge on a dirty worktree. In run 01M0SS23MJM8972CBJD0SP7T4Q, tester@2 (922ms) and evidence@2 (384ms) re-ran on a byte-identical worktree because implementer@2 was verification-only by design; the unconditional edge from implementer to tester wastes one gate plus evidence pair per procedural resubmit, and the waste scales with gate weight.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-6bbe","title":"Clear review_feedback in the reviewer Approved JSON template","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:44.372Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:44.372Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md, add \"review_feedback\": \"\" to the Approved JSON template so the verdict flip resets stale rejection text. In run 01M0SS23MJM8972CBJD0SP7T4Q, planner@3 still carried the full 1.6KB cycle-1 'changes requested' feedback alongside review_verdict=approved, letting dead instructions leak into the next seed's re-plan. Complements fabro-5870 (closeout clearing): this triggers at verdict flip, mid-loop.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-8d61","title":"Document glob_filter glob syntax in the planner prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:44.521Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:43:44.521Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, note that the grep tool's glob_filter expects a glob (e.g. *.go), not a bare filename like main.go. In run 01M0SS23MJM8972CBJD0SP7T4Q, planner@1 burned two empty grep calls (seq 58-59 with glob_filter: \"main.go\") plus a recovery find/head call; the prompt note prevents those wasted turns independently of fabro-8354 landing ripgrep in the image.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-b065","title":"Blank stale seed context keys when routing Tracker empty","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.701Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.701Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, extend the 'Tracker empty' JSON contract to also blank current_seed_id/title/brief and implementation_summary (it already clears review_verdict). In run 01M0T9B7T6XNM1D7JNY35Y6H8K the final planner pass closed seed fabro-8208, routed 'Tracker empty', yet its prompt still carried the dead seed's brief (1.6 KB) and implementation_summary (1.7 KB) as blob refs after budget demotion. Expected effect: the closing planner pass stops hauling stale seed context — fewer blob round-trips, smaller preambles, lower risk of the evidence-starvation pathology noted in the graph comments. Not a duplicate of fabro-b382, which covers prose duplication and sd call rules, not the context_updates key contract.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-d936","title":"Make seeds-cli exit non-zero on errors (exit 0 masks failed tracker writes)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.848Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-04T22:54:20.848Z","description":"@os-eco/seeds-cli v0.5.15 prints errors like 'error: unknown option --format' to stdout with exit_code 0 — observed at events seq 62-63 of run 01M0T9B7T6XNM1D7JNY35Y6H8K when planner@1 ran sd update with --format json; only the model's text inspection caught the failed write. Change: seeds-cli exits non-zero and prints errors to stderr. Expected effect: removes a silent-corruption path for tracker writes (any exit-code-checking consumer or gate currently reads failure as success) and eliminates the observed wasted retry. Prompt-side syntax pinning is already covered by fabro-1399; this is the orthogonal CLI-side fix.","labels":["revision"]}
